<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding an unknown constant in a discrete probability distribution formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Otieno models the number of goals (\(X\)) his school's football team scores per match. The discrete random variable \(X\) takes the values 0, 1, 2, 3, and 4.</p>
<p>He determines that the probability distribution is given by the algebraic formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( P(X=x) = k({@expr@}) \)</p>
<p>where \(k\) is an unknown constant.</p>

<p><b>a) </b> For this formula to represent a valid probability distribution, the sum of all probabilities must equal 1. Find the exact value of the constant \(k\).</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(k =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Using your complete formula, calculate the probability that the team scores <b>at least {@t@} goals</b> in a match (\(P(X \ge {@t@})\)).</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P(X \ge {@t@}) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Finding the Constant \(k\)</b><br>
A valid probability distribution function (PDF) must sum to 1 over all possible values of \(X\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \sum_{x=0}^{4} P(X=x) = 1 \)</p>
<p>We substitute each value of \(X\) (0, 1, 2, 3, 4) into the formula \(k({@expr@})\) and add them together:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( k({@val0@}) + k({@val1@}) + k({@val2@}) + k({@val3@}) + k({@val4@}) = 1 \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( {@sum_coeffs@}k = 1 \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ k = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Cumulative Probability</b><br>
"At least {@t@} goals" means \(X \ge {@t@}\). We find the sum of these specific probabilities up to the maximum value of 4:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X \ge {@t@}) = {@prob_sum_string@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X \ge {@t@}) = {@target_coeff_sum@}k \)</p>
<p>Substituting our known value of \(k = {@ta1@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(X \ge {@t@}) = {@ta2@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
